WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.370
Political rookie Emmanuel Macron is leading
the polls and is tipped to be France's next

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.800
president.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.000
The 39-year-old’s meteoric rise has shaken
the political establishment...

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.350
while also being its last hope.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:27.789
His centrist, pro-European, open-border views
stand in stark contrast to the rising voices

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:30.380
of Europe's resurgent far right.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:34.870
This is how Macron’s unabashed ambition
and drove him from star pupil,

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:36.790
to banker, to political rebel

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:40.060
and now to the hot favourite to lead France.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.559
Macron was raised in the town of Amiens, two
hours north of Paris…

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:49.809
This is the house he grew up in.

00:00:49.809 --> 00:00:54.570
The eldest of three children from a family
of doctors, he attended a Jesuit school.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:59.180
A precocious kid, he preferred the company
of teachers to other pupils.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:02.769
And it was at school that he met his future
wife.

00:01:02.769 --> 00:01:05.810
Brigitte Auziere was coach of the drama club.

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:09.140
They worked closely together to re-write a
school production

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:10.140
He was 16.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.380
She was 40, and married with three children

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:20.759
Gossip about their relationship began to spread
and Macron left Amiens to finish high school

00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:23.920
at an elite establishment in Paris.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.479
Auziere followed later to teach

00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:29.620
And the pair married when Macron was 30.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.909
After school he attended university in Paris,
studying Philosophy,

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:38.659
then went to the prestigious National School
of Administration, a breeding ground of the

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:40.890
French elite.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:45.810
He works for four years as a high level bureaucrat
at the Ministry of Economy, before moving

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:49.159
to the renowned investment bank Rothschild.

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:59.240
Macron was quickly parachuted into managing
a massive acquisition

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.249
When the deal went through, he got a big payout.

00:02:03.249 --> 00:02:08.720
Then in 2012 Macron was offered a position
working with the new president, and a personal

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.319
friend, Francois Hollande.

00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:16.010
Two years later, Hollande gave him the prestigious
position of Minister of Economy.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:18.500
He was 36.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:23.230
But by now Hollande’s public approval rating
had fallen to historic lows.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.030
Macron threw himself into a plan to loosen
economic regulation…

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:31.440
With testy exchanges in parliament.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:38.660
But the reforms were disliked and the legislation
had to be forced through parliament, sparking

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.270
protest.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:46.880
Macron increasingly criticised the government
but still enjoyed the president's support.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.740
Then last year he launched his own political
movement, En Marche, or On the Move

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:54.070
thrusting him into the national spotlight.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:58.800
He’s really come out of nowhere, three years
ago Emmanuel Macron was barely known to the

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.410
general public and here he is today on the verge of becoming President

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.410
That's Mark Deen

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:09.730
I’m the deputy bureau chief at Bloomberg News in Paris and I’m on the campaign trail with Emmanuel

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:10.730
Macron

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:13.930
The youthful contender was seen as a presidential
long shot

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:18.290
When he started his movement everyone, including many journalists

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:21.110
including myself, said oh well that's pretty cute

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:25.150
and it's a nice effort but he's not going to be president

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:30.390
But borrowing from US President Barack Obama’s
election playbook, he took to social media

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:34.460
and ran a large grass-roots campaign.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:39.750
By the time France went to the polls for the
first round of voting in April he had successfully

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.740
reinvented himself.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:47.300
He was no longer the free market reformer
working under a failed President...

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:50.220
but a new voice in politics.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.820
He secured the 
most votes of any candidate in the first round,

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.720
putting him into a runoff with another political
outsider,

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:18.039
the far-right Marine Le Pen.

00:04:18.039 --> 00:04:21.549
Still it’s not all smooth sailing into the
The Élysée Palace -

00:04:21.549 --> 00:04:26.169
Macron has many critics on both sides of the
political spectrum.

00:04:26.169 --> 00:04:30.060
But against a far right candidate who wants
to leave the EU,

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:33.569
will voters on the left and right swing behind
Macron?

00:04:33.569 --> 00:04:38.879
“The answer is that polls currently show
that is what will happen.

00:04:38.879 --> 00:04:45.009
However this election is not over, abstention
is key and anything can happen,

00:04:45.009 --> 00:04:47.160
we’ve seen it with Brexit, we’ve seen
it with Trump.

